/-!
# Infinite sequences of point blowups and nonsingular formal arcs

An infinite sequence of blowups at closed points with unchanged residue fields, whose
exceptional divisors are locally cut out by the successive transforms of a single element of the
initial local ring, comes from a nonsingular formal arc: the limit of the local rings is a
complete discrete valuation ring, and that element is a uniformizer.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.PointBlowupSequence` records the schemes, the closed centres, the blowup
  identifications and the transition maps of an infinite sequence of point blowups.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_nonsingularFormalArc_of_pointBlowupSequence` constructs the complete
  discrete valuation ring, the arc to it, and the compatible lifts of the arc to every stage.

## Implementation notes

The exceptional-divisor condition is read in the local ring at each selected point: the extended
maximal ideal of the preceding point is generated by the image of one element of the initial local
ring. Nonsingularity of the arc is the statement that this element generates the maximal ideal of
the valuation ring.

The limit of the local rings is formed as a limit in `CommRingCat` over the poset `ℕ`, which
avoids choosing a presentation of the inverse limit; the uniformizer and the local structure are
read off from the explicit description of its elements.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BG2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BG2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

